From 9ea0c09985c9150477a1358c7abfc7a7926fe1fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:25:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cheeseburger: WLAN streams on the ANOC2 SMMU, WLFW freeze
 bisect knobs

0150 reached WLAN ON (mission) and the SoC froze ~5 s later with no panic and no USB: the WCN3990 firmware DMAs through the ANOC2 SMMU (0x16c0000, SIDs 0x1900/0x1901) that nobody set up. sweet_wsmmu.c ports topaz 0123 smmu_identity(): read-only dump of the valid SMRs, then an untranslated context bank (SCTLR.M=0, from CB4) for the WLAN streams before step 11, read back and logged (the boot chain owns this SMMU: qcom,skip-init). sGFSR and the bank FSR/FAR are logged when they change, plus a heartbeat every 500 ms after FW_READY. sysctl kern.sweetwlfw_smmu (default 1) and kern.sweetwlfw_upto (0 mission, 1 stop at FW_READY, 2 stop after WLAN_CFG).
---
 bsd/conf/files        |   1 +
 bsd/dev/sweet_glink.c |   4 +
 bsd/dev/sweet_mlink.h |   6 ++
 bsd/dev/sweet_wlfw.c  |  24 +++++
 bsd/dev/sweet_wsmmu.c | 211 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 246 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 bsd/dev/sweet_wsmmu.c

